e a better chance to draw B9. Or if they discard B8, they can get B9.\n\nAnother angle: the hand has a meld of W1-2-3. If they can form another Chi in W suit, like W6-7-8, but missing W7. Unshown W7 has 2 left. If they can get W7, that would help. But they don't have it now.\n\nAlternatively, the hand could aim for a Full Flush in one suit. For example, if they focus on W suit. They have W1-2-3 (meld), W6, W8, W9\u00d72. If they can form W6-7-8 and W9-9-9, but missing W7 and W9. But unshown W7 has 2, W9 has 4. Possible, but not sure.\n\nAlternatively, focus on B suit. B4, B7, B8. If they can get B5-6-7 and B8-9-10, but that's not feasible. Or B7-8-9 if they get B9.\n\nAnother possibility: the hand could be aiming for All Terminals and Honors. But they have W6, W8, which are not terminals. So probably not.\n\nLooking at the scoring patterns, maybe the hand is trying for a Full Flush (all one suit). If they can form all W tiles. They have W1-2-3 (meld), W6, W8, W9\u00d72. If they can get W7 and W9. Let's see:\n\n- Melds: W1-2-3, W6-7-8, W9-9-9. Plus a pair of W9. That would be four melds and a pair. That would be a Full Flush, which is 24 points. That's possible. But need to get W7 and W9. The unshown W7 has 2 left, W9 has 4. So if the player can draw W7 and W9, that would work.\n\nAlternatively, if they discard B4, they can focus on W suit. But if they discard B4, they still need to get W7 and W9. If they discard B4, the remaining tiles are W6, W8, W9\u00d72, B7, B8, F4, J1. But B7 and B8 are in another suit. Not helpful for Full Flush.\n\nAlternatively, if they discard B7 or B8, they can focus on W and B suits. But not sure.\n\nAnother angle: the hand has F4 and J1. If they can form a pair with one of them, but only one each. Unless they draw another.\n\nAlternatively, if they discard F4 or J1, maybe to get more suited tiles.\n\nLooking at the valid actions, the best move might be to discard a tile that's less useful and allows for more flexibility. For example, B4 